# Aang's Iceberg: "Waterbend {3}: Sacrifice this enchantment. If you do, scry 2." With the Iceberg cast on turn 3 with no
# target ("up to one"), on turn 5 Bot1 pays for the ability and Bot2 responds by destroying the Iceberg with Disenchant.
# The ability resolves with nothing to sacrifice, so there is no scry (CR 608.2c, 701.21a). That is proved by the scry
# line that follows it: Bot1's Preordain then casts and its own scry 2 takes `Arrange(Forest | Mountain)`, so the Forest
# is drawn; had the Iceberg scried first it would have taken that line, left Preordain's scry at its default, and the
# Mountain would have been drawn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Mox Pearl
Aang's Iceberg
Plains
Mox Sapphire
Preordain
Island
Swamp
Mountain
Forest
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Disenchant
Plains x20

